<<~ ahu slot=`#/p27-wiring-step-3-build-seat-lane-p27-wire`>>

! P27 wiring, step 3 — build seat (Sol), lane p27-wire

Conductor: Lares-Kiaʻi. Same wall as steps 1-2: workspace-write in /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/p27-wire/wt, network off; you EDIT, the conductor runs tests and commits. Steps 1 and 2 ran before a launcher fault (now cured) stopped each at 600 s mid-work; their edits stand UNCOMMITTED in the tree (`git diff --stat` shows ~34 files). Read both briefs whole: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/p27-wire/seats/sol-1/brief.md and /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/p27-wire/seats/sol-2/brief.md. Step 2's owed list is YOUR owed list. Measure where step 2 left each item (it was threading an `IslandAudienceContext` through the island pool when it stopped) and finish it; do not restart from scratch, and do not undo step 1/2 work without naming why.

Finish, in order: (1) the audience fork (the CAS audience reads off the asking island's relation; daemon island in-process, pool wiki island its plane, herm shore and HTTP /cas world; an unreadable relation refuses by name), with its red and control; (2) genesis and engine blobs at boot (measure, decide, prove); (3) the fixtures in packages/lararium-mesh/tests/one-composer.test.ts and lar-vessel.test.ts; (4) typecheck node and browser (`tsc -p … --noEmit`).

WRITE YOUR FINAL MESSAGE as soon as the edits stand, before any long check. Hand back outcome first: files changed, each crossing's wiring (file:line) with its audience source, each red/control file and what it asserts, forks decided and why under the house laws, drift found, and the exact test files the conductor runs alone (marking browser-runner ones).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* A read seat writes no file: its final message carries the hand-back. Any other seat writes `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

